lor:#5a6bff;color:#fff;font-weight:700}\n  .btn.primary:hover{background:#3a4bff}\n  .btn-row{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}\n  .board-holder{position:relative}\n  .overlay{position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(7,10,24,.74);backdrop-filter:blur(3px);border-radius:10px;z-index:10}\n  .overlay.hidden{display:none}\n  .overlay-box{text-align:center;padding:18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;align-items:center}\n  .overlay-box h2{margin:0;font-size:26px;color:#fff;text-shadow:0 0 12px #5a6bff}\n  .overlay-box p{margin:0;color:#c3cbf2;font-size:13px}\n  .t-controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:6px}\n  .tbtn{background:#1f2650;color:#e8ebff;border:1px solid #3a4578;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 4px;font-size:12px;cursor:pointer}\n  .tbtn:hover,.tbtn:active{background:#2b3568}\n  @media (max-width:780px){\n    .layout{flex-direction:column;align-items:center}\n    .panels{width:100%;flex-direction:row;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center}\n    .panel{flex:1;min-width:104px}\n    .help{display:none}\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <h1>俄羅斯方塊 <span>TETRIS</span></h1>\n  <div class=\"layout\">\n    <aside class=","reasoning_content":"The user says the Russian Tetris (俄羅斯方塊 = Tetris) has errors when opened in browser: no complete HTML (maybe truncated: length). They want a complete HTML file output. I'm a front-end engineer, output only fixed complete HTML file in a ```html code block, CSS and JS in same file, no external resources.\n\nI need to produce a complete Tetris game in a single HTML file. Let me write a robust, self-contained Tetris.\n\nRequirements:\n- Full HTML document with DOCTYPE, html, head, meta charset, title, style, body, script.\n- Tetris game: canvas-based, colors, rotation, clearing lines, scoring, levels, game over, start/pause.\n- No external resources.\n\nI'll design: grid 10 columns x 20 rows, cell size 30px => canvas